title: Liberty Comes from Christ: Why Nations Rise and Fall
description: Posts from the channel on why nations rise and fall: liberty comes from Christ, God judges individuals by grace and nations by their works, and the means of government is incidental to the hearts of the people.
output: lessons/posts/pulled-liberty-comes-from-christ.html

# From the posts of 2023-12-29 (two), 2023-12-30, 2024-01-21 and 2024-04-25
# (studies/data/notes/pulled-liberty-comes-from-christ.html), in the author's words, with the review's cuts and fixes.

=== Introduction
--- Liberty Comes from Christ [title]
overline: From the channel
heading: Liberty Comes from Christ
sub: Why nations rise and fall. Everything is downstream from a people's relationship with God.
refs: Deuteronomy 12:8-9; Deuteronomy 28:1-2; 1 Samuel 12:23; 2 Chronicles 7:14
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the slides. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

=== Right in his own eyes
--- Instruction to us
kicker: Deuteronomy 12
p: This is not only instruction to the children of Israel, but to us as saved Christians.
scripture: Deuteronomy 12:8-9 | mark: every man whatsoever is right in his own eyes
p: The blessings of liberty come from those who believe on the Lord, know His word and follow it. Not from every man doing what is right in their own eyes.

--- Freedom comes from Christ
lead: Freedom comes from Christ, and the blessings that follow come from a people made righteous in the blood of the Son, obeying the will of the Father, filled with the Spirit.
p: A people who know the judgment of God, His mercy and longsuffering, loving good and abhorring evil.
refs: John 8:36; Galatians 5:1; Romans 12:9

--- To their own destruction
p: Removing God from this, or worse, turning Jesus into a false version of Him, inventing a Christ that pleases their itching ears, has been a disaster.
p: And now that we are a few generations away from the bedrock of faith the people built upon, they seek to "conserve" not that which is God's, but the lusts of their own hearts. To do that which is right in their own eyes. And they do it to their own destruction.
refs: 2 Timothy 4:3-4; Judges 21:25

=== God puts government in place
--- Not libertarian
lead: There are Internet theologians who claim that the OT law of the newly founded Israel was libertarian. That we should as Christians be libertarian. But that is a lie.
p: God has laws. God puts government in place. The leaders may follow the god of this world. They may be wicked, as their people are wicked. But they exist to enact judgment.

--- As the people, so the rulers
panel-warn: Weak | when God seeks to overthrow a people.
panel-warn: Tyrants | when the people turn from God.
panel: Less authoritarian | when the people can govern themselves, because they seek first the things of God.
refs: Matthew 6:33; Isaiah 3:4

--- Regardless of the state
p: That is the biblical truth, given repeatedly in Scripture. We as believers are to bring others to believe, regardless of the nature of the state. Regardless of economic systems or repression. Rejoicing in tribulation. Winning souls.
lead: Because the more godly the people, the greater the blessings of liberty. The freer we are. The more moral and just.
refs: Romans 12:12; Proverbs 14:34

--- Turn not to the right hand nor to the left
scripture: Proverbs 4:25-27 | mark: Turn not to the right hand nor to the left

=== Downstream
--- Everything is downstream
lead: Everything is downstream from a people's relationship with God. That is the lesson of the Bible.
panel: Individuals | God judges individuals by His grace and their faith. One is the individual soul liberty we have as believers.
panel: Nations | And nations by their works. The other by how godly a people are.

--- Free speech and gun rights
p: Free speech in a society that is Christian enough that non-believing members feel uncomfortable challenging basic decency and morality, works. Free speech where Christians are a looked down upon remnant, doesn't.
p: Gun rights in a world where most people are God-fearing is a good thing. It keeps the bad guys afraid.

--- Do that which is good
scripture: Romans 13:1-7 | mark: do that which is good, and thou shalt have praise of the same
take: The blessings that allow these freedoms come from liberty in Christ. Do that which is good, and you get them. Simple as.

=== Blessings and curses
--- Deuteronomy 28
kicker: Deuteronomy 28
stat: 14 | verses blessing them for obeying
stat: 40 more | verses cursing them if they depart from God's commands
p: 40 more verses cursing the children of Israel if they depart from God's commands than the 14 blessing them for obeying.
refs: Deuteronomy 28:1-2; Deuteronomy 28:15

--- The same promise
p: The conditions placed on the people in the law were that it be well with them, and the same promise applies to us today.
p: We have the advantage of the total knowledge of God in His scriptures, the earnest of His promise in our hearts, the Spirit testifying within that we are saved, sealed unto redemption. We have the one sacrifice of Christ Jesus, and the one additional command to go out into the world and bring people to Christ with the word of truth.
refs: Ephesians 1:13-14; Ephesians 4:30; Hebrews 10:12; Mark 16:15

--- The blessings of liberty
p: A nation that calls itself His, where a majority are faithful brethren, receives the abundance of His blessings. The blessings of liberty.
p: America was one such nation for a time. And that is the excellence that people speak of, it came from God to a humble and separated people. And in just a few generations that was squandered as we turned to the left and the right and allowed Idolatry to take root in the land.

--- All those curses have come to pass
p: And now all those curses have come to pass. Strangers in the land eat of our stores. They are lifted up over us. All that we set to do are destroyed and perish quickly. We have a people smitten with madness, and blindness and astonishment of heart. Our sons and daughters given to another people as fodder for their wars.
refs: Deuteronomy 28:43-44; Deuteronomy 28:20; Deuteronomy 28:28; Deuteronomy 28:32
lead: We have become an astonishment, a proverb, and a byword among all nations.
refs: Deuteronomy 28:37

--- Would not obey
big: Deuteronomy 28:63 | mark: the LORD will rejoice over you to destroy you
p: And the Lord that blessed America is rejoicing over our destruction because we who call ourselves by His name would not obey the voice of the Lord our God.

=== The hearts of the people
--- Incidental to the hearts of the people
kicker: 1 Samuel 12
lead: One of the takeaways to the story of Israel, from the patriarchs, Moses and Joshua, the judges and kings, is that the means of government is incidental to the hearts of the people.
p: That how they are ruled is not as important as their faith in God and their not turning aside to vanity, to the gods of this world. Not falling into Idolatry. Not rejecting His promise or the inheritance He has established for us. Obeying the commandments and law He has given us that it be well with us and we live long in the land He has appointed for us.
refs: 1 Samuel 12:20-21; Deuteronomy 5:33

--- None of it matters
p: The same is true for us today. For all the political discourse on the proper means of government, the economic system that's used, the means of deciding leadership, the false binary choices we are given...none of it matters if we are not a godly people.
lead: And if we are, it will not be a terror for us, but against those who would do evil.
refs: Romans 13:3

--- Men of God
p: We need men of God who stand on His word, preaching against sin. Who say;
big: 1 Samuel 12:23 | mark: I will teach you the good and the right way
p: preaching the whole word of God. In season or out of season. And the people who call themselves by His name to follow Him in all things.
refs: 2 Timothy 4:2

--- Calling for a king
tile: 1 | Calling for a king. [[1 Samuel 8:5-7]]
tile: 2 | Bringing the ark to battle without the Lord being present. [[1 Samuel 4:3]]
tile: 3 | Offering our own sacrifices and not accepting His. [[1 Samuel 13:11-13]]
p: But the solutions offered by so many boil down to calling for a king. For bringing the ark to battle without the Lord being present. For offering our own sacrifices and not accepting His. Not repenting to the Lord that He may deliver us.

--- The old paths
lead: We have the government we deserve.
p: The evil done to us is the result of turning away from the straight paths, the old paths that God has made for us. Turning to the left or to the right.
refs: Jeremiah 6:16; Proverbs 4:25-27
big: 2 Chronicles 7:14

=== The answer
--- The answer to the problem
p: Winning souls and living Godly, raising Godly children, and assembling together to edify one another, training up those who can go out and do likewise, studying to be approved by God, able to rightly judge, is the answer to the problem.
p: Our judging the fatherless and taking care of our widows indeed. Bringing hope to the hopeless. Staying spotless from the sins of the world.
refs: Proverbs 11:30; Hebrews 10:24-25; 2 Timothy 2:2; 2 Timothy 2:15; 1 Timothy 5:3

--- To set at liberty
scripture: Luke 4:18-19 | mark: to set at liberty them that are bruised
scripture: James 1:27

--- No political solution [title]
heading: No political solution
sub: There is no political solution to a spiritual problem.
refs: 2 Chronicles 7:14; John 8:36
